# <%= projectName %>

Web-components SPA walking skeleton scaffolded by keel — hexagonal, framework-free:
the browser and the DOM API are the framework.

## Layout

```
design-system/   — the project's design language: atomic design on top
                   of @rgoussu.dev/planks (layout primitives + token
                   scale), with the project's tokens, atoms and
                   molecules; domain-blind by construction
domain/
  domain-api/    — ports, commands, read models; zero deps, compiles
                   without the DOM lib ("the domain never touches the
                   browser" is a tsc error, not a convention)
  domain-core/   — services and stores; its `exports` map exposes only
                   factory entry points, so deep imports fail at
                   module resolution
application/
  web-app/       — the deployment unit: index.html + main.ts (the
                   assembly point) + port-bound custom elements
infrastructure/  — driven adapters wrapping browser capabilities
                   (clock in `commons`; gateway/storage as they appear)
```

The walls are held by the workspace itself: package dependencies point
inward only, and each package's `tsconfig` sets its own `lib`.

## Wiring

No mediator. Each use case is a driving port delivered to elements over
the [WCCG Context protocol](https://github.com/webcomponents-cc/community-protocols/blob/main/proposals/context.md):
`main.ts` constructs adapters and domain factories, registers one
`context-request` listener, then defines the elements — provider first,
definitions last. Cross-cutting concerns decorate the factories at the
assembly point.

## Design system

Atomic design and the hexagon compose: the hexagon organises the
application, atomic design organises the inside of the driving adapter.
The line through the hierarchy is **port-awareness**:

- **Sub-atomic** — [planks](https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/planks)
  layout primitives (`<stack-pk>`, `<box-pk>`, …) and its token scale,
  plus the project's brand layer in `design-system/src/tokens.css`.
- **Atoms & molecules** — `design-system/src/atoms/`,
  `design-system/src/molecules/`: attributes in, `CustomEvent`s out,
  never a domain import. The package declares no dependency on the
  domain, so a domain-aware "atom" fails at module resolution.
- **Port-bound organisms** — `application/web-app/src/components/`:
  where ports meet design-system children; they push read-model state
  down as attributes and translate child events up into commands.
- **Templates & pages** — the shell's `index.html` and its router as
  it grows.

Everything renders in the light DOM: planks styles by tag-scoped
stylesheets injected into `document.head` (they would not pierce a
shadow root), and the design system follows the same convention.

## Run

```sh
<%= pm %> run dev        # Vite dev server for application/web-app
```

## Test

```sh
<%= pm %> test           # domain + fake contract tests in Node; design-system
                   # component tests under happy-dom
<%= pm %> run typecheck  # per-package tsc — enforces the lib walls
```

Port-bound organisms are tested in a real browser against the domain's
in-memory fakes; add a Vitest browser-mode setup to
`application/web-app` when the first organism with real logic appears.

## Build

```sh
<%= pm %> run build      # application/web-app/dist — static files, ready to serve
```
